                        <h3>Maria Garcia</h3>
                        <p class="meta">45 years old • London, UK</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <span class="treatment-tag">Lumbar Spine Surgery</span>
                <p class="story-excerpt">An accountant whose career was threatened by chronic back pain that had plagued her for over a decade. After being told surgery would cost £35,000 privately in the UK, with an 18-month wait on the NHS, Maria sought alternatives.</p>
                <div class="story-highlight">
                    <p>"I was taking 8 painkillers a day just to get through work. Now, two years later, I'm completely pain-free and running 5k three times a week."</p>
                </div>
                <p class="story-excerpt">Maria traveled to Shanghai Ruijin Hospital where Dr. Liu performed a minimally invasive lumbar discectomy. The cutting-edge procedure, unavailable at this price point in Europe, cost just £10,000 including all travel arrangements.</p>
                <div class="savings">Saved £25,000</div>
                <a href="maria-garcia.html" class="read-more">Read Full Story →</a>
            </div>

