                <div class="faq-item">
                    <h4>Is medical treatment in China safe?</h4>
                    <p>Yes. Many Chinese hospitals are JCI-accredited (Joint Commission International), meaning they meet the same standards as top US and European hospitals. Look for hospitals with international patient departments and English-speaking staff for the safest experience.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <h4>How much can I save by having surgery in China?</h4>
                    <p>Savings typically range from 50-80% compared to Western countries. Common procedures like knee replacements cost £6,000-8,000 in China vs £20,000-25,000 in the UK. Heart surgery can cost $10,000-15,000 vs $100,000-200,000 in the US.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <h4>Do I need a visa for medical treatment in China?</h4>
                    <p>Yes, you'll need a visa. Medical tourism visas (M visa) are available for patients seeking treatment in China. Most medical tourism agencies assist with the visa application process and can provide invitation letters from Chinese hospitals.</p>
                </div>
